/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:8:V.1 audit (2026-05-28) caught `mathematica_transliteration` on 9 of 12 dirty stages (164, 166, 169, 170, 171, 172, 173, 174, 175) — the highest v2 share, reflecting V.1's uniformly mechanical linear/rational algebra. **7 received independent-route additions.** **164** — `Series`/`Coefficient` perturbation of the explicit healing-locked product monomials extracts the two log-channel coefficient vectors and reconciles them plus the compressed `delta_perp`, machinery absent from the SymPy hand-form. **166** — `Inverse[Mmat]` matrix-inverse derivation of the 4x4 drift inversion plus a `Total[(Mmat.solVec - obs)^2]` round-trip, distinct from the shared `Solve`. **170** — replaced `Series`/`Coefficient` linearization with `D[...,eps]/.eps->0` and removed the SymPy-style `du2sym`/`dP0sym` placeholder idiom (direct `Solve[du2==du2Hyb,dkappa]`). **171** — the directive's first route was tautological (`zCombFormula` rebuilt from the same `D[z2,...]` as `zCombExact`, caught by verification as `needs_rework`); reworked to a native-typed collected closed-form target (load-bearing against the engine's own `D[]` bundle) PLUS an independent `Series`-coefficient second route per bundle. **172** — implicit differentiation of the defining relations (`Solve`/`D` on `u2 D0 + D2 = 0` etc.) replaces the `Normal[Series[...]]/(eps*lam)` quotient. **173** — direct `Coefficient[Series[...],eps,1]` extraction replaces `(D[...,eps]/.eps->0)/lam` and removes the `d41Hidden` general-solve. **174** — `D[b0Eps,eps]/.eps->0` (and z0/n0 analogues) reconstructs the BdG/Maxwell/transfer differentials instead of re-typing the SymPy closed forms. **2 accepted as policy mirrors** (no forced rewrite, per this policy's default that transliteration is expected): **169 F2** (grouped invariant `(dX.gMat.dY)/5` — the F1 per-coefficient numeric checks vs the paper Family-1 weights restore substantive second-engine coverage) and **175 F3-step3** (the `dlogSeries` route; banner + the F1 Sigma_N fix were applied, step 3 left as a mirror). Transliteration share for V.1 = 9/12 = 75% dirty — the highest v2 share, above IV.6's 60%. **Orchestrator-catch in rework**: stage 171 (above) — the directive's `D[...]`-based reconstruction was algebraically identical to `zCombExact`, making the bundle checks `X-X`; the verifier flagged `needs_rework`, and the orchestrator restored a genuine collected-literal target and added a `Series` cross-route, re-verified clean (23 PASS). Also stage 166's round-trip vector residual `{0,0,0,0}` failed `expectZero` (which tests `res === 0`, False for a list) -> scalarized to `Total[(...)^2]`.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:18:IV.2 audit (2026-05-27) caught `mathematica_transliteration` patterns on 5 of 7 dirty stages (105 — full `.wl` rewrite with structurally distinct path: unfactored ratio + `Apart` round-trip check + `SeriesCoefficient` operator form + `Reduce`-over-reals for chi_Q + polynomial inversion of `Λ·Y = -3` for the deformed branch; variable names changed (no `yRet`/`lamDef`/`yDef`/`omegaQ`/`sigmaCan`). 106 — full `.wl` re-author starting from the retarded one-pole form `Y_ret(omega) = 3/4 + (1/4)/(1 - omega^2/OmegaQ^2 - i chi_Q sigma_Q^can omega^5)`, series-expanding to omega^7 to show next odd term is at O(omega^7), with no `nqGeneral`/`k0`/`k2`/`k4`/`gamma5` intermediates; closure to N_Q=1 via source-map relation. 109 — linearization rewrite via numerator/denominator-separate series + `Series[1/denominator]` inversion + multiply, solving `chiSeries - 1 == 0` directly for `a5` without the `coeff = (chiSeries - 1)/eps` intermediate. 111 — added independent chi_Q^mix re-derivation block bypassing the L0/L5 extraction (geometric-series form of the pole alone), plus new `expectZero["chi_Q^mix routes agree", chiMix - chiMixAlt]`. 112 — added independent Stage-92 linearized cross-check extracting `(a_0, a_5) = (3 sigma, -sigma gamma)` from solB's deformation and solving the preservation condition `a_0/3 + 9 a_5 = 0` for `gamma_W = 1/9`, an algebraically distinct route from the chi_Q-based solve). Transliteration share for IV.2 = 5/7 = 71% dirty; higher than IV.1 (4/11 = 36%) but several of these were borderline mathematical mirrors where the structural rewrite added genuine engine independence rather than pure renaming. **No new pitfall candidates** from IV.2 — all orchestrator-direct edits applied first-attempt clean. But pitfall #11 (PASS-line discipline) was **re-confirmed prominently**: 108 F2 caught `chiArg /. beta -> 1 - 1` parsing as `(chiArg /. (beta -> 0))` because Mathematica `Plus`/`Subtract` binds tighter than `Rule`. The buggy assertion `0^5 = 0` had been silently passing on every prior run; only the auditor's structural read caught it. Fix: `(chiArg /. beta -> 1) - 1`. This is a **persistent class of silent-pass bug** — any directive instructing Codex to write `expr /. var -> value <op> rest` must use explicit parentheses around the `Rule`, or the parser bends the bracket. Augment pitfall #11 with: Mathematica `/.` (ReplaceAll) binds looser than `+`/`-`/`*`/`/`/`^` but Rule binds even looser; always parenthesize `(expr /. rule)` when followed by arithmetic.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:20:IV.1 audit (2026-05-27) caught `mathematica_transliteration` patterns on 4 of 11 dirty stages (091 — full series+Solve+assertions port; closed with an independent partial-fraction recombination block using `Together` not `Series`. 092 — full Series+Solve[branch==0, kg0] port; closed with a restructure to work in dimensionless `(eps_2, eps_4)` variables from the outset, deriving `K_0 = 4 K_2^2/K_4` directly without `Solve[]`. 095 — line-by-line Schur-complement port; closed with an independent Schur derivation block via `Solve[D[Lq, gSym] == 0, gSym]` from the bilinear L action, before the existing series machinery. 097 — line-by-line algebraic choreography port; closed with an independent route via `SeriesCoefficient[kbarCons[w], {w, 0, n}]` series extraction rather than direct definitions, and `gamma5Target` derived via `9 k0Target/(32 omegaQ^5)` not `9 k2Target^(5/2)/k0Target^(3/2)`). **100 F4 (`mathematica_transliteration` for the outgoing-normalization series choreography) was marked BLOCKED in the directive as a design-level rewrite needing user direction; user picked Cluster B (c) which strengthens the substantive closure derivation but does not authorize a full second-engine rewrite. 100's load-bearing closure assertion is now non-tautological on both engines (`mhat_0^2 Gamma_5 = Gamma_5_target` imposed as the observable condition, derives `mhat_0^2 chi_Q N_Q = 1`), but the upstream series-expansion choreography still follows SymPy step-for-step.** Transliteration share for IV.1 = 4/11 = 36% dirty; lower than III.3 (4/7 = 57%) but higher than III.5 (3/5 = 60% with 1 won't-fix). **No new pitfall candidates from IV.1** — all orchestrator-direct edits applied first-attempt clean; verifier PASS-line counting confirmed expected substantive checks across all 12 stages (e.g., 094 Mathematica 34 PASS lines = 30 orthogonality + 1 Y00 norm + 3 static-limit; 097 Mathematica 9 PASS = 2 series-equiv + 1 Gamma5 closed form + 1 geometric target + 1 Gamma5_target + 4 R_i).
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:32:III.1 v2 re-audit (2026-05-26) caught *new* `mathematica_transliteration` findings in stage 043 (full Sections 1-5 port) and stage 045 (coefficient-chain port). Stage 043's fix introduced a separate pitfall (NEW pitfall #7 candidate): **primitive-vs-derived substitution**. The directive's F2-Insertion2 numeric-point sign anchor prescribed substituting `sigma_0=0, rho_0=1` symbolically, but the Mathematica expression's primary symbols are the primitive couplings `gB, gU, gS, gR, gW, kU` — `sigma_0` and `rho_0` are derived quantities (`sigma_0 = gU·gS/(kU·gB)`, `rho_0 = gU·gR/(kU·gW)`). Symbolic substitution on derived names doesn't reduce the primitive expression. Iter2 fix: substitute on primitives that realize the derived value — `gS → 0` for sigma_0=0, `gW → gU·gR/kU` for rho_0=1. Defense: when a directive prescribes `subs(<derived>, value)`, lift to the primitive symbols that realize the derived value. Promote to `codex.md` if recurs.
